# Source: naoki66/ImmortalWrt-for-Gemtek-XR1710G 625-net-pcs-airoha-update-USXGMII-rate-adaptation-on-link-up.patch
#   （Ryan Chen <rchen14b@gmail.com>，2026-03-06）
# Upstream: n/a（作者自持；与本仓 9029/9038 同域但机制不同——本补丁修的是"速率块被 else 分支关死"的确定性缺陷）
# Reason: 上游 airoha_pcs_link_up() 把整段 USXGMII 速率自适应（RATE_UPDATE_MODE /
#   FORCE_RATE_ADAPT_MODE）关在 `neg_mode != PHYLINK_PCS_NEG_INBAND_ENABLED` 的 else 分支里；
#   而 USXGMII 走 in-band 自协商 → **该段永不执行**，速率切换后寄存器停在上一档速率。
#   本补丁把 USXGMII 速率块移出 forced-mode-only 分支；SGMII in-band FIFO 阈值与
#   SGMII/1000BASEX forced 速率配置仍按各自 neg_mode 门控（语义不变）。
#   直接关联本仓 2026-09-08 实机记录"PHY 宣告 10G、AN 落 2.5G"（验收 d25a994）——
#   10G LAN2 无法升速的确定性候选根因之一。
# 验证：naoki66 基线上 clean applies（Hunk #1 succeeded at 694, offset -53，本轮 B-1 实测）；
#   本仓构建树未实跑内层应用 → 故列 #EXP。实机判据：强制 10G↔2.5G↔1G 切换后 ethtool 速率
#   与实际协商一致、RATE_UPDATE_MODE/FORCE_RATE_ADAPT_MODE 随速率更新。
From: Ryan Chen <rchen14b@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: airoha: fix USXGMII rate adaptation on speed changes

The USXGMII rate adaptation code in airoha_pcs_link_up() is inside an
else branch that only executes when neg_mode is not
PHYLINK_PCS_NEG_INBAND_ENABLED. However, USXGMII uses in-band
autonegotiation, so this code path is never reached on speed changes.
The RATE_UPDATE_MODE and FORCE_RATE_ADAPT_MODE registers remain
configured for the previous speed.

Fix this by moving the USXGMII rate adaptation block out of the
forced-mode-only branch so it runs regardless of the negotiation mode.

Signed-off-by: Ryan Chen <rchen14b@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/target/linux/airoha/patches-6.18/625-net-pcs-airoha-update-USXGMII-rate-adaptation-on-link-up.patch b/target/linux/airoha/patches-6.18/625-net-pcs-airoha-update-USXGMII-rate-adaptation-on-link-up.patch
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/target/linux/airoha/patches-6.18/625-net-pcs-airoha-update-USXGMII-rate-adaptation-on-link-up.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,148 @@
+From: Ryan Chen <rchen14b@gmail.com>
+Date: Thu, 06 Mar 2026 12:00:00 -0600
+Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: airoha: fix USXGMII rate adaptation on speed
+ changes
+
+The USXGMII rate adaptation code in airoha_pcs_link_up() is inside an
+else branch that only executes when neg_mode is not
+PHYLINK_PCS_NEG_INBAND_ENABLED. However, USXGMII uses in-band
+autonegotiation, so this code path is never reached on speed changes.
+The RATE_UPDATE_MODE and FORCE_RATE_ADAPT_MODE registers remain
+configured for the previous speed.
+
+Fix this by moving the USXGMII rate adaptation block out of the
+forced-mode-only branch so it runs regardless of the negotiation mode.
+The SGMII in-band FIFO threshold adjustment and the SGMII/1000BASEX
+forced-mode speed configuration remain gated on their respective
+negotiation modes as before.
+
+Signed-off-by: Ryan Chen <rchen14b@gmail.com>
+---
+ drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha-common.c | 127 +++++++++++---------
+ 1 file changed, 69 insertions(+), 58 deletions(-)
